//! The `border-inline-start-width` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property
//! defines the width of the logical inline-start border of an element, which maps to a physical
//! border width depending on the element's writing mode, directionality, and text orientation. It
//! corresponds to the `border-top-width`, `border-right-width`, `border-bottom-width`, or
//! `border-left-width` property depending on the values defined for `writing-mode`, `direction`, and
//! `text-orientation`.
//!
//! Initial: medium. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - medium: Same as `3px`. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/line-width
//! - thick: Same as `5px`. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/line-width
//! - thin: Same as `1px`. See
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/line-width
//!
//! Grammar: <line-width>
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-borders-4/#propdef-border-inline-start-width
//!
//! Author guide:
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/border-inline-start-width
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

